description:
Destination-neutral zonal aggregation. Loads a published GeoZarr dataset over a time range and aggregates its variable within each GeoJSON feature, area-weighted, using the chosen method. The result is a vector cube with one value per feature and time step, at the dataset's native temporal resolution.

The workflow saves nothing itself: the caller decides where the result goes. A pipeline saves it through its destination's export plugin; a process graph can pass it to `save_result` in any tabular format. `aggregate_to_dhis2_json` and `aggregate_to_chap_csv` are the same computation with a fixed output format.

Usage:

{
  "agg": {
    "process_id": "aggregate_by_features",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "era5land_precipitation_monthly",
      "temporal_extent": ["2025-01-01", "2025-12-31"],
      "geometries": { "type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [ ... ] },
      "method": "mean"
    }
  },
  "save": {
    "process_id": "save_result",
    "arguments": { "data": { "from_node": "agg" }, "format": "CSV" },
    "result": true
  }
}
